The call-site change for the SPARSE height planes, plus the shim removal.
=======================================================================

    git apply docs/overlay-sparse-planes.patch

APPLY THIS AS PART OF THE MERGE, NOT AFTER IT. master builds WuchangMinimap and
markers_test with /WX (warnings as errors, added on the fix-release branch), and the
compatibility shim this patch deletes is marked [[deprecated]] - so on a /WX build the
three call sites in overlay.cpp are ERRORS until this lands. That is deliberate: the
shim is empty, and a build that merely warned would ship a minimap with no floor on it.

WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT
----------------------------------
src/overlay.cpp is owned by another workstream in this release, so the branch that made
the height planes sparse (src/mapdata.*, review item C.14) could not edit it. Everything
else is done, committed and green; these are the last hunks.

WHAT CHANGED UNDER IT
---------------------
The height planes were eight dense `width * height` uint16 arrays - 343 MB for chapter
1, of which 74 % was the code 0, "no surface here". They are now 128-px blocks with an
int32 index per slot, and only the non-empty blocks are allocated: 86 MB for chapter 1,
47..74 MB for chapters 2-5. An absent block reads as code 0, so no ANSWER changes.

What does change is that a row of the picture crosses several blocks, so there is no row
pointer to hand out. `hm.plane[k].data()` + `plane + sy * hm.width` becomes
`hm.gather_row(k, sy, col_x, w, scratch)`, which fills one destination row of height
codes - the same `w` reads per plane per row the dense version did, plus one index
lookup per 128 columns - and returns false when the row carries no surface at all, which
lets the slicer skip most rows of the deeper planes outright.

THE HUNKS
---------
  src/overlay.cpp
    1. `SliceScratch` gains `std::vector<std::uint16_t> gather` (and clears it).
    2. It is sized next to `col_x`, which is already per-slicer.
    3. `slice_region()`'s plane loop: `plane_empty(k)` instead of `plane[k].empty()`,
       `gather_row()` instead of the row pointer, and the inner loop reads
       `gathered[col]` instead of `src[col_x[col]]` - so the `sx < 0` test disappears,
       because a column outside the asset gathers as code 0.
    4. The slicer self-test's "find a lit pixel" scan becomes `hm.first_lit(0, ...)`,
       which the block index answers directly instead of striding over 43 MB.
  src/mapdata.hpp
    5. Deletes the deprecated, empty `plane[]` shim.
  src/mapdata.cpp
    6. Deletes the "overlay.cpp still reads the dense plane[] member" log line.

VERIFIED: with this patch applied, build.ps1 is clean - no C4996, no other warning - and
markers_test passes 10 275 checks. Without it the tree still builds (three C4996
warnings naming the call sites) but the minimap draws no floor, and mapdata.cpp says so
in the log at every chapter load.

STILL NEEDS AN IN-GAME CHECK (nothing here can be verified without launching):
  * the minimap and the full map still draw the floor the player is standing on with the
    storeys above/below dimmed - i.e. gather_row() agrees with the old row pointer on the
    real asset at a real position. markers_test proves it byte-for-byte on chapter 1's
    eight planes, but not through the slicer.
  * the slice timing in the F2 dev overlay. The block index adds one lookup per 128
    columns and skipping empty rows should make the deeper planes cheaper, so the ~4 ms
    slice should not get slower. Any stall belongs to the loop thread, never to Present.
  * the height-slicer self-test line at the main menu ("slice: self-test sliced a ...
    window") must still report opaque pixels - it now finds its probe pixel through
    first_lit().

